rem Polynomials with at Least One
rem Integer Root
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=269
rem Count the n up to 10^K whose digits,
rem taken as the coefficients of a
rem polynomial, give one with an integer
rem root

use bits
use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option K integer = 16

rem The roots can only be 0 and -1 to
rem -9. Root 0 is a last digit 0, and
rem 10^K is one of these n. For the
rem others, by inclusion and exclusion
rem over sets S of roots, count the
rem digit strings with last digit 1 to 9
rem whose polynomial P is divisible by
rem G, the product of x + r for r in S.
rem Dividing from the low end, P = G Q
rem gives q[i] = (p[i] - sum g[j]
rem q[i-j]) / g[0] so the state is the
rem last d quotient coefficients, d the
rem degree of G, packed in base B.
rem Digits run for K places, then d
rem zeros, and the quotient must end at
rem 0. Equal states merge by sort.
Base = 2001
Off = 1000
Total = 10 ** (K - 1)
Zero = array 0
Pos = 0 to 8 array
for Mask in 1 to 511
  Sel' = (Mask shr Pos) band 1 equal 1
  Rs = (1 to 9 array) filter Sel array
  G = array 1
  for R in Rs
    Up' = concat G Zero
    Sh' = concat Zero G
    G = Up * R + Sh
  end
  D = G len - 1
  Lead = G 0
  Gw = G drop 1
  Pw = Base ** (0 to (D - 1) array)
  Key0 = ((Pw - Pw + Off) * Pw) sum
  Keep = Base ** (D - 1)
  Keys = array Key0
  Cnts = array 1
  for I in 0 till (K + D)
    N = Keys len
    if N equal 0
      break
    end
    Col' = Keys reshape N 1
    Lag' = (Col // Pw) mod Base - Off
    Back = (Lag * Gw) sum axis 1
    Tail = Keys mod Keep
    NK = array shape 0 fill 0
    NC = NK
    Lo = 0
    Hi = 9
    if I equal 0
      Lo = 1
    end
    if I at least K
      Hi = 0
    end
    for P in Lo to Hi
      Acc = P - Back
      Q = Acc // Lead
      Fit = Acc mod Lead equal 0
      Fit = Fit and (Q at most Off - 1)
      Fit = Fit and (Q at least 1 - Off)
      Nk' = (Q + Off) + Base * Tail
      Na' = Nk filter Fit
      NK = concat NK Na
      Ca' = Cnts filter Fit
      NC = concat NC Ca
    end
    Keys = NK
    Cnts = NC
    if Keys len equal 0
      break
    end
    Ord = Keys argsort
    Ks = Keys Ord
    Cum' = (Cnts Ord) scan +
    Tl' = Ks drop 1
    Nx' = concat Tl (array -1)
    Last = Ks not equal Nx
    Ke = Ks filter Last array
    Ce = Cum filter Last array
    H = Ke len
    Hd' = Ce take (H - 1)
    Pc' = concat Zero Hd
    Keys = Ke
    Cnts = Ce - Pc
  end
  Hit' = Keys equal Key0
  Done' = Cnts filter Hit
  Count = Done sum
  Sign = 1 - 2 * ((Rs len + 1) mod 2)
  Total += Sign * Count
end
Answer = Total
Answer print
